        "original_id": "4c8f8242-49f2-57d8-9d35-f5611cd9fc91",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Milium, Eucommia, Eucommia ulmoides\n- Places: Eurasia, North America, North Africa, China\n- Concepts: grass family, fossil record, conservation status, cultivation, traditional Chinese medicine\n\nFacts:\n- Milium, also called milletgrass, is a genus of plants in the grass family found in Eurasia, North America, and North Africa.\n- Eucommia is a genus of small trees now native to China, and its fossil record shows that it once had a much wider distribution.\n- Eucommia ulmoides is the only living species in the genus Eucommia.\n- Eucommia ulmoides is near threatened in the wild.\n- Eucommia ulmoides is widely cultivated in China for its bark.\n- Eucommia ulmoides is highly valued in herbology, including traditional Chinese medicine.",
